WEBVTT

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.160
After his amazing win at
the fight of the century

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:17.000
the new champ, Mac Rosario,
got surprising news this morning.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.620
According to ROSCO, the next
challenger they're choosing

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.300
is none other than "Gearless" Joe himself!

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.130
That was indeed a surprise,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:34.050
considering the last place we saw
Joe was in the audience of that match.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.680
According to the announcement, the
official offer to Joe has yet to be made.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.690
But why did the champ choose
"Gearless" Joe now?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.770
Mac Challenges the Legend For His Next Match!!

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:50.320
To Mac--no. To everyone
who loves Megalo-boxing,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.530
"Gearless Joe" is someone special.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.620
Mac's wish was to stand in
the same ring as the legend.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.040
I figured that was the least
I could do to repay him.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.590
Not to mention, I'm sure
you're all dying to see

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.340
a match between Mac and Joe.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.300
If we do get to see
this match come to life,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.050
it'll truly be a match between
the new and the old.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.390
It will be a match between
the strongest and a legend.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.890
Isn't that awesome, Joe?
You're gonna do the match, right?

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.980
When you do, don't forget to
give me the exclusive interview!

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.060
Pretty sure that's some kind of mistake.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:31.610
What? You heard them. This is an
official announcement from ROSCO.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.240
The rest is up to you, Joe.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.080
Come on. It doesn't matter
how much you fix this place up.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.080
Team Nowhere isn't Team Nowhere
until you get into that ring, Joe!

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:47.290
Then again, I guess you have a point.
This is pretty sudden.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.840
Sorry.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.670
Nah. This is your decision, Joe.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.680
But if you change your mind,
make sure you give me a call.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.720
I'll be waiting.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.850
Mac Challenges the Legend For His Next Match!!

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.850
Does This Mean a Comeback for 'Gearless' Joe?!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:17.110
"Team Nowhere"

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.890
MEGALOBOX 2

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.590
We'll have to thank Sakuma.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.760
Yes. He keeps coming up
with something new.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.010
"An Incomplete Device"
"ROSCO's Brain Chip's Abnormal Behavior"

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.350
And thanks to him, the damage
from this thesis was minimal.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.430
"Mac Challenges the Legend
For His Next Match!!"

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:13.480
We won't know if they're nothing but
rumors until we properly look into this.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.320
They are nothing but rumors.
Just malicious and false accusations.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.570
There haven't been any issues in the
reports ROSCO's been giving us, has there?

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.200
Correct. But according to our findings,

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.330
it became clear that they were
intending BES for military use.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.750
At this point,

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.500
I believe it wise to rethink
our dealings with ROSCO.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.460
Rethink?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.130
What?

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.800
I agree with Ms. Asamoto.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.470
Shirato had just shifted its
focus to the medical field.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.430
We should not be working with a company
whose focus is to work with the military.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.480
Are you implying we cancel
this deal with them, then?

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.350
Yes.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.440
That's insanity.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.360
Our value will go down 50% without ROSCO.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.820
That may be true if we're
looking at the small picture.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:02.570
But--

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.070
Madam President.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.750
You made a decision to not allow our
Gears to be used for military use

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.500
and made us lose our contract
with the military,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.670
which made us go through
a financial crisis.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:16.920
What would've happened to this company
without the partnership with ROSCO?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.630
You haven't forgotten this, have you?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.050
Their reactions are as we predicted.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.050
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.600
But the fact that Mr. Sakuma
has chosen Joe for this event

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.520
might prove that he is also a bit
panicked about this thesis.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.230
That may be so, but our
hands are currently tied.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.320
We will need to find some proof
that supports Mikio's claims.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.950
It's always so hard to
breathe in this room.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.160
Ma'am...

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.170
Let us get a bite to eat.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:00.550
We might get some good ideas
if we get some fresh air.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.380
You're right.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.770
You'll need to turn in your
reports by this weekend.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.310
Don't expect any credits if they're late.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:28.700
The thesis you published about BES...

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:33.790
I'm sorry. "Thesis" was a bit generous.
It was basically a sci-fi novel.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.960
"ROSCO Labs Head of Development"

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.880
Our company asks that
you retract your claims.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.340
And if I refuse?

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.970
Then we will have to take legal action.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.220
Well, that might be a problem.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.300
Whether it be donations to
support research, or taking in interns,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.930
our company has always had a good
relationship with this school.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.480
We would hate to see this
ruin our relationship.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.020
I guess it's been five years now.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.900
In your Gear
engineering outline, you wrote,

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.200
"Machines will always break someday.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:13.580
Developers must always be thinking
about what to do after they break."

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:18.080
Machines will always break. I don't
see how BES is any exception.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:25.420
I'm shocked that you
remember me, Professor.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:29.640
Well, it was my first
lecture at this school.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.900
I didn't understand how the
world worked back then.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:43.650
You can't create anything
with backwards ideas.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.650
The only true path to the future

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.240
is to continue facing forward
and challenging yourself.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.290
Even if you know that's dangerous?

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:57.710
I believe that the future
can only get better.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:01.540
I hope you'll consider
what we talked about.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.880
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:07.260
I think the moment you stop because
you realize you've made a mistake,

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.970
is also taking a step towards the future.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.940
Please excuse us.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:37.830
I was worried about Liu. I'm glad
he agreed to speak with me.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:42.460
You two settled things in the ring.
You shouldn't worry about it.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:44.460
My head gets it.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.630
This guy's a bit more stubborn, though.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.800
This is my wife Maya, and my son Miguel.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.260
He's somewhat of a miracle child.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.270
He was born with a serious disease,

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.980
but he proved to be a true fighter.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:06.440
The reason I step into that ring
is to see my son smile.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.240
Why'd you choose me?

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:15.740
You'll always be a champion to me.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:22.290
I'm still living the dream that
you showed me to this day.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.220
I hope we'll hear a favorable
answer regarding the match.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.510
He's just like me.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:42.940
We want to prove that we're the real deal
in that ring by fighting "Gearless" Joe.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.610
I haven't made up my mind yet.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.780
Oh, you'll do it.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:53.780
The most insulting thing you could do to
me is run from Mac and still fight me.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.110
Get better soon, Liu

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.080
Back in that ring,

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.920
I knew Mac Time was coming but
couldn't do anything to stop it.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.930
Be careful, Joe.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.430
Mac's no ordinary fighter.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.030
Guess tomorrow's the big day.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.240
Yeah.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.620
What's the matter, Joe?

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.490
You look down in the dumps.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.960
Nah.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:48.710
Those kids will understand
how you feel someday.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.300
Never forget this, Joe.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.180
No one can ever take away...

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.640
...the time we spend on this earth.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.010
That's never gonna change.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.850
So keep fighting until the end.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.570
I will always be with you.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.280
I promised Pops.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:15.990
I told him I'd stay here and fight.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.370
It's not over...

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.250
But it can't be over!

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:25.710
Please! I'm begging you!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:36.470
Back then, the reason you
accepted the fight with Liu

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.890
wasn't to pay for Mr. Nanbu's
medical expenses.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.100
Was it?

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.310
I wanted to prove to everyone
that it wasn't over.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:50.440
That would be the light of hope we'd
need to guide us after Pops died.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.400
Or at least, that's what I was hoping for.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.440
And how did that turn out for you?

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.070
You're the one who destroyed everything!

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:02.830
Gym Nowhere died a long time ago!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:07.000
After Pops died,
I figured if I disappeared,

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.380
they could move forward again.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.130
But I was clearly wrong.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:18.760
I should've stayed here no matter what.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:23.560
If you're going to fight Mac again to
bring back the light that was lost,

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.930
that's just your hubris speaking.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.940
Are you really going to repeat
what you did five years ago?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.280
I met this guy.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:42.200
You'll always be our champion.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.870
I'm going to continue dreaming
this dream that you showed me.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:53.250
It's because of him that I
was able to come back home.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.760
Mac reminds me of that guy.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:03.510
There's still something I have to do.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.520
I know what's most important to me.
I won't misjudge that again.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.110
Joe!

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.980
It came! It actually came!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.990
What did?

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:20.900
An official offer from ROSCO!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:34.750
I was contacted as the acting
representative for Team Nowhere,

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.090
and asked what you might think.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.420
The match will be an exhibition match

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:42.260
and will take place in two months.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.800
Don't do it.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:49.680
You saw that last match.
You're no match for him.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.520
Do you plan on getting revenge for Liu?

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.980
I'm sick of your vain heroism.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.690
Yuri.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.950
That's not it.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.240
I've always fought for myself.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:09.290
That's how it's always been
and that's how it'll always be.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.460
Do as you please.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.370
Affordable Chinese Food Ichibanya

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.670
Man, Joe's just so amazing.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.750
Mac Challenges the Legend For His Next Match!!

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:22.090
He's gonna do this match, right?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:26.100
He hasn't answered yet, but of course.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:30.220
I wonder if there's anything we can
do to help. Like the good ol' days.

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:35.940
Does Sachio know about this fight?

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:41.360
"Does This Mean a Comeback
for 'Gearless' Joe?!"

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.030
"Does This Mean a Comeback
for 'Gearless' Joe?!"

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.080
He's going to do this fight.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.800
This fight with Mac.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:04.930
I'm hoping you'll be by his side.

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:07.010
I'll be fine.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:13.310
Ever since he lost to me,
he's been suffering all alone.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.480
You're the only one
who can lift that curse.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:19.020
Joe doesn't matter anymore.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.280
The reason I returned to
Megalo-boxing is you.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:28.160
Is that why you're going to
feel like you're to blame forever?

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.950
It's not anyone's fault
that I ended up like this.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.710
It's because I chose this path.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.960
Don't ever forget this, Yuri.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.340
You didn't choose me.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:43.710
I chose you.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:55.430
I want to go further. Further than you.
Further than Joe.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:16:01.150
So teach me what true Megalo-boxing is.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:03.400
Yeah? Then how about you enlighten me?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.570
Not just two guys beating on
each other. You show me...

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.700
...what true Megalo-boxing is.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:13.200
Yuri.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.290
Joe needs you right now.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.890
How long have you been here now?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.520
Six months.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.980
Think you can finally win
some matches now?

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:46.990
Put me in more matches!
I've been itching for a good fight!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:50.530
Oh? And why do you want to fight so badly?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:54.830
Don't give me that shit. You know
it's because I need the money!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:56.160
So how much do you want?

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.120
I can have it prepared immediately.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:05.710
In return, you're going to be doing
fixed fights in my ring until you die.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:10.050
If that's what you want, I'll grant
your wish right here and now.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.690
Get the hell out!

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.940
I need to talk to you, Sachio.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.360
There's nothing to talk about.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.110
I want to fight Mac.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:36.410
I want you to fight by my side again.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.410
This doesn't concern me.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.290
You're on your own.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.090
Sachio.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:52.930
When you asked me to teach you
Megalo-boxing, I never asked you why.

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:58.720
Because whatever that may be,
I was hoping it'd help you cope.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.190
But the thing is, Sachio...

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:03.560
...you'll never be Joe.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:08.070
You should have your own path.

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:11.780
And that's right here.
I've made up my mind.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:15.950
Then get in that ring and
settle things that way.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.450
While you're at it...

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.120
...you can put what's most
important to you on the line.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.380
Our home.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.550
If you win, I'll leave.

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:32.840
I'll never come back here again.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.260
But if I win...

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.180
...you'll leave the ring.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:41.980
Let's do this.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:47.290
Let's stop this, Sachio.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.800
Piss off.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.880
The match isn't over yet!

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.510
Quit being so selfish!

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:03.810
But I am selfish.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.190
I did all of this on my own.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.740
I'm the one who decided to fight Liu.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.030
I'm the one who abandoned
all of you and ran away.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.870
So it's not your fault!

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.260
God damn it...

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:49.350
We had always put everything
on the line for his dream.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.860
That's how we became a family.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:58.030
He's just like you. He wants to do
nothing more than protect all of you.

00:20:58.030 --> 00:21:00.450
You're not part of our family anymore.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.240
Don't ever show your face
around here again.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.540
Why...?

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:19.090
Why'd you leave us?!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.010
Joe!

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:31.100
Sachio.

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.110
Let's go home...

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:42.530
...Sachio.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.500
That kid's nothing but trouble.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:59.010
But I made sure he got where
he needed to be, Mr. Nanbu.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:06.930
I'm fine now. I can walk on my own.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:08.180
Good.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:11.100
We'll be waiting outside.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.310
Yeah.

00:22:32.710 --> 00:22:33.920
Joe!

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:36.880
Wake up, Joe!

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:40.590
Joe!
